  ✓ Stage 2: check contract, program fidelity, translation identity, and differential behavior
  ✓ Stage 3: reconstruct semantics/proofs cleanly and execute generated semantics
  → Stage 4: assess claim adequacy and real-program pinning
  • Stage 5: inventory and audit every syntax/function/rule
  • Stage 6: create and run a fresh false non-vacuity mutation
  • Stage 7: account for proven versus assumed boundaries and write final REVIEW.md
